  "raw_text": "## RESEARCH & DEVELOPMENT\n\nINTERNAL CORRESPONDENCE\n\nTO: MR. P. H. HARPER\n\nCC: MR. T. E. SANDEFUR\n\nDR. P. L. AULBACH\n\nSECRET. Do Not Copy Or Make Notes Of This Page And Do Not Give Any Of The Information Contained In This Document To Anyone Except In Conformance With The Moorgate Secrecy Protocol.\n\nFROM: MR. D. S. ROTH\n\nDATE: JANUARY 13, 1983\n\nSUBJECT: KENT 80/KS TAR REDUCTION - FINLAND/907\n\nRef S/R 107/82\n\nAfter evaluations and rejections of tar reduction samples 49B, 50B, and 51B we have reviewed deliveries and designs of several KENT products to find one which meets the 10.0 mg/cig. (DPM) and 0.7 mg/cig. nicotine constraints.\n\nWe propose the following two trials.\n\n\n<table border=1 style='margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;'><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'></td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Trial 1</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Trial 2</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Blend (%) :</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'></td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'></td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MGLF-31</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>69.9</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>69.9</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Oriental</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>10.3</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>10.3</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MRT</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>5.0</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>0.0</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>F.C. WTS</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>14.8</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>19.8</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Final Casing</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MGE-651</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MGE-651</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Final Flavor</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MGE-603</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>MGE-603</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Cigarette Paper</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Current KENT</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Density</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>KENT GOLDEN LIGHTS (Less 2%)</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Filter Tow</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>KENT GOLDEN LIGHTS</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Plugwrap</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>9500 Coresta</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Tipping</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>1100 Coresta MMP*</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>•Vent Target</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>---</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>42-44%</td></tr></table>\n\n $ ^{*} $We recommend the micromechanically perforated tipping because this is the only type of tipping with essentially invisible perforations at this high porosity level.\n\nD. S. R.\n\n\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"imgs/img_in_image_box_1767_2759_2217_2846.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" width=\"17%\" /></div>\n\n\nDSR/bfw\n\nJAN 1 8 1983",
